      mastery_orientation: [70, 0.58, "s", "A"],
      // [src_haydn_britannica, src_haydn_austriaforum | 1761-1790 | encyclopedia + biography] Britannica describes almost daily rehearsals, composing most of the music the court required and supplying more than 150 pieces for the prince's baryton over about thirty years of service; Austria-Forum counts 104 symphonies, 83 quartets, 52 piano sonatas and many other works. The documented volume and routine support steady working discipline; no source describes his personal work schedule, so the score stays in the clear-lean band.
      discipline: [72, 0.58, "d", "A"],
      // [src_haydn_austriaforum, src_haydn_britannica | 1760s-1801 | biography + encyclopedia] Austria-Forum lists symphonies, string quartets, piano sonatas, about thirty operas, fourteen masses, four oratorios and divertimenti; Britannica adds baryton music, church music and operas for the court. The range of genres is directly documented; the quality across them (the operas especially) is not assessed by the sources, so the score is not raised.
