      // [src_haydn_historytoday, src_haydn_britannica, src_haydn_austriaforum | 1784-1795 | magazine piece + encyclopedia + biography] When the Esterhazy cuts of 1790 came, he accepted Salomon's invitation and went to London at 58 without English, and promptly began English lessons; Britannica says he revised Il ritorno di Tobia in 1784 in awareness of changing sensibilities and calls him flexible and receptive to new ideas; Austria-Forum says the chapel's 1795 re-establishment brought him back to a new duty. The sources disagree on whether his salary was cut, and none states his reasons, so the lean is a strong inference.
