      // [src_pv_encyclopedia, src_pv_biography | 1954-1963 | reference + popular biography] Six years of training with few results while he worked as a schoolteacher and insurance salesman, and the Biography.com account (from his own autobiography) of deciding to quit before his voice improved. The slow route to a professional debut is documented; the quitting episode is self-reported and the obstacle he credits is a vocal-cord problem, so it is not treated as a character judgement.
