      // [src_tao_imu, src_tao_clay, src_tao_sciam, src_tao_paw | 2004-2015 | award body + institution + news + magazine] The Fields laudation says the Green-Tao result on arithmetic progressions in the primes 'shows great originality and insight' and describes work on Kakeya, wave maps and the Horn conjecture in an area far from his own; the Clay report calls his work astonishing in depth and originality; in 2015 he proved the Erdos discrepancy conjecture after years of failed attempts by others and Gil Kalai said he was completely confident of it. The strongest praise is from award bodies and friendly profiles, but the outcome (accepted proofs of long-open problems) is independently verifiable. SELF-CALIBRATION (agent): reviewed as a top-risk row; kept, since the 2015 result has an independent expert's confirmation, not only citation language.
