      // [src_tao_imu, src_tao_clay, src_tao_paw | 2000-2019 | award body + institution + magazine] The laudation lists work in harmonic analysis, nonlinear partial differential equations, combinatorics and additive number theory, and notes the Horn conjecture result (compared to a novelist suddenly producing the definitive novel in another language); the Clay report counts more than 140 papers ranging from dynamical systems to representation theory, algebraic geometry and compressed sensing; PAW adds compressed sensing in imaging and Navier-Stokes. All within mathematics, but unusually wide, and consistently reported across institutional and press sources. SELF-CALIBRATION (agent): reviewed as a top-risk row; kept because three independent descriptions list specific different fields and results. RUBRIC_CORRECTION (lead review, before eligibility): cross_domain_range lowered from 82 / 0.7 to 78 / 0.62 because same award-citation and press-profile concentration; the breadth is documented but the stated score and confidence were above the evidence.
